add('3',5.5,'Combinatorics',r'A $5\times5$ board is covered with copies of the tetromino whose cells have coordinates $(0,1),(1,0),(1,1),(2,0)$. Rotations and reflections are allowed; every copy lies on the board. Copies may overlap, but no cell may belong to more than two copies. What is the maximum number of covered cells?','An ordinary checkerboard does not give the required obstruction. A four-parity colouring bounds the number of pieces, then a separate overlapping construction must attain the bound.',['colouring','covering','extremal construction'],notes='The tetromino is described by cell coordinates to preserve the original diagram exactly without relying on a picture.')
